/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493614 #edb/ref 1080 "quartic binomial" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493614 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493614 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "8caae5ad-2091-5a94-9de8-16bbe05ea834" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493617 #edb/ref 1080 "Cubic binomial" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493617 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493617 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "8ee88caf-fa42-587f-9b4e-37e2a9c5dac2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493654 #edb/ref 1080 "II only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493654 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493654 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "a66f3f1f-29ec-5be2-8bc5-722c8e836b92" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493686 #edb/ref 1080 "Cubic trinomial" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493686 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493686 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "b5c26456-8a47-5d01-856e-a94ad2152272" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493753 #edb/ref 1080 "I only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493753 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493753 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "e4b1e4de-0805-5bfa-8e45-f45979420ad8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493792 #edb/ref 1080 "I, II, and III" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493792 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493792 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "f7a93d32-18e7-5f8e-961d-886b53773bcf" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493827 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186493442 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493827 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186493477 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493827 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186493489 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493827 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186493506 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493827 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186493614 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493827 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493827 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493827 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186493489 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493827 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "5cfb5c23-969b-59ed-8fd1-dd67557eb34a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493830 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186493420 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493830 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186493546 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493830 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186493557 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493830 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186493617 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493830 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186493686 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493830 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493830 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493830 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186493686 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493830 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "61ac3cf1-ce85-58c6-8c68-c0b075726ad0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493853 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186493537 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493853 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186493585 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493853 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186493654 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493853 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186493753 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493853 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186493792 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493853 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493853 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493853 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186493537 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493853 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "9a727332-6125-5bf9-8eee-55ebc8cbefb8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493921 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186493853 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493921 #edb/ref 1069 "q-152221" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493921 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493921 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following statements are true? \n\nI. The sum of $4{x}^{2}+1$ and $2{x}^{2}$ is a binomial.\n\nII. The sum of $3{x}^{2}-2x$ and $5$ is a binomial.\n\nIII. The sum of a binomial and a monomial is **sometimes** a binomial." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493921 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4a6f2377-d91b-5967-99d3-f6f62abbce5f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493921 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. We have\n\n$$\n(4{x}^{2}+1)+(2{x}^{2})=6{x}^{2}+1,\n$$\n\nwhich is a binomial.\n\n- Statement II is false. We have\n\n$$\n(3{x}^{2}-2x)+(5)=3{x}^{2}-2x+5,\n$$\n\nwhich is *not* a binomial (it's a trinomial).\n\n- Statement III is true. The sum of a binomial and a monomial *could be* a binomial (see, for example, statement I). \n\n However, the sum of a binomial and a monomial is *not always* a binomial (see, for example, statement II). \n\n So, the sum of a binomial and a monomial is *sometimes* binomial.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493944 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186493827 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493944 #edb/ref 1069 "q-111223" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493944 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493944 #edb/ref 1071 "Categorize the polynomial ${z}^{5}-3z$ based on its degree and the number of terms it has." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493944 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a6b20681-3c0e-56d8-a0d2-12a0033bb72d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493944 #edb/ref 1074 "The polynomial ${z}^{5}-3z$ has two terms, so it is a binomial.\n\nAlso, its degree is $5,$ so it is a quintic.\n\nTherefore, the polynomial is a quintic binomial." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493954 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186493830 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493954 #edb/ref 1069 "q-51576" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493954 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493954 #edb/ref 1071 "Classify the polynomial $5{y}^{3}-2y+1$ according to its degree and the number of terms." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493954 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "becc645b-7ce0-5458-abaa-ac04d1cbd85e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493954 #edb/ref 1074 "The polynomial $5{y}^{3}-2y+1$ has three terms, so it is a trinomial.\n\nAlso, its degree is $3,$ so it is a cubic.\n\nTherefore, the polynomial is a cubic trinomial." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493977 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186493994 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493977 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "05338efe-276c-51da-8655-6d896721903f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493977 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186493954 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493992 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "33040ec4-d764-5460-b879-febde2296a30" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493992 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186493921 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493994 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186493992 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493994 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "39e3b333-15cb-5985-99ff-5688251c0604" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493994 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186493944 #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
